From 3d1ea49286880b701e82fb38ac19d3c44ef99616 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Wang <sean.wang@mediatek.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 17:41:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7925: stop init retries on hung bus

Stop retrying hardware init once the bus is marked hung.

The control path is no longer usable at that point, so more retries only
issue failing device accesses, including MCU commands or register
operations, and delay teardown. Exit early and let the failed device be
torn down quickly.

Signed-off-by: Sean Wang <sean.wang@mediatek.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260613224131.2396026-2-sean.wang@kernel.org
---
 mt7925/init.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7925/init.c b/mt7925/init.c
index 741e38b2..e39f1c1d 100644
--- a/mt7925/init.c
+++ b/mt7925/init.c
@@ -128,10 +128,18 @@ static int mt7925_init_hardware(struct mt792x_dev *dev)
 	set_bit(MT76_STATE_INITIALIZED, &dev->mphy.state);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < MT792x_MCU_INIT_RETRY_COUNT; i++) {
+		if (atomic_read(&dev->mt76.bus_hung)) {
+			ret = -EIO;
+			break;
+		}
+
 		ret = __mt7925_init_hardware(dev);
 		if (!ret)
 			break;
 
+		if (atomic_read(&dev->mt76.bus_hung))
+			break;
+
 		mt792x_init_reset(dev);
 	}
 
